{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Justice, justice shall you pursue.</b> When you appoint judges for yourself — you who select the judges — choose the most righteous of judges, even if they lack other qualities desirable in a judge, such as perfection of property and perfection of physique, as it says: אַל תַּבֵּט אֶל מַרְאֵהוּ וְאֶל גֹּבַהּ קוֹמָתוֹ (1 Samuel 16:7)." "<b>That you may live and possess.</b> You will have need of this all the more in the land, for this deficiency will prevent possession of it, as it says: בַּעֲוֹן בִּצְעוֹ קָצַפְתִּי (Isaiah 57:17)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:36.729231945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}